{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "USBLC6-2SC6",
 "kind": "tvs",
 "manufacturer": "STMicroelectronics",
 "title": "USBLC6-2: two-line low-capacitance ESD protection with VBUS clamp, SOT23-6L and SOT-666",
 "source": {
  "document": "Doc ID 11265",
  "revision": "Rev 5, October 2011",
  "pages": 14
 },
 "summary": "A monolithic ESD protection array for two high-speed data lines plus a supply rail. Each line is steered by a pair of small diodes, one to GND and one to VBUS, and a single 6 V breakdown diode sits between VBUS and GND, so a strike on either line is clamped to the rail. Line capacitance is 2.5 pF typical to GND; the listed uses are USB 2.0 up to 480 Mb/s, USB 1.1 low and full speed, 10/100 Ethernet, SIM cards, video lines and portable electronics. It meets IEC 61000-4-2 level 4 at the device and comes as the USBLC6-2SC6 in SOT23-6L and the USBLC6-2P6 in SOT-666.",
